  "prompt": "In which month did each subscription see its latest recorded MRR change, and how many subscriptions is that per month? Use recorded_at, which is Brussels local time, as stored; the month is the first day of its month. Every event counts, opening events included. Each subscription counts once, in the month of its change with the latest recorded_at. When two changes of a subscription tie on recorded_at, the lower event_id is kept. Return two columns, in this order: last_change_month and subscriptions. Return one row for each month that holds some subscription's latest change. Any row order is fine.",
